-- machine_power_kw) below has been corrected against a second
-- transcription of the same source screenshots (press_machine_staging.json)
-- -- the original standard_press_machine_data.json had every one of its 16
-- machines' physical/capex block reassigned to a DIFFERENT machine's values
-- (a row-alignment error), confirmed by diffing both files field-by-field.
-- User confirmed press_machine_staging.json's pairing is correct. Direct/
-- Indirect OH and price for these 4 tiers now exactly match Progressive Die
-- Press's own tiers of the same tonnage -- consistent with a shared
-- reference-benchmark convention across the Press/Forming family, not a
-- further conflict. The other 12 machines (already-known Progressive Die
-- Press/Tandem Press duplicates, never promoted) are unaffected.
--
-- SECOND CORRECTION (2026-08-27, after this migration had already been run
-- live once): a 4th transcription (std_press.json) of these same 4 machines
-- matched the ORIGINAL standard_press_machine_data.json pairing exactly --
-- tying the vote 2-2 against the "corrected" pairing above (which had 2
-- files agreeing: press_machine_staging.json and stage_press.json). Direct/
-- Indirect OH were identical across every transcription throughout and were
-- never in question -- only the physical/capex block (price, press force,
-- dimensions, power) was ever in dispute. User decided the tie in favor of
-- the ORIGINAL pairing; the values below are reverted back to it. Migration
-- 586 updates the already-promoted mhr_records rows to match (this file's
-- own values only matter for a future fresh-DB run). Step 1b's separate
-- 'Standard Press (staging)' audit copy of press_machine_staging.json is
-- deliberately left untouched below -- it is a faithful record of that one
-- file's own transcription, not a claim about which pairing is correct.
-- ============================================================================

